      "role": "user",
      "content": "The diagrams below show two electrochemical cells in which carbon electrodes are used. In cell A, concentrated copper (II) chloride solution is used and in cell B, liquid aluminium oxide is used.\n\nWhat type of electrochemical cell, ELECTROLYTIC or GALVANIC, is shown above? Give a reason for the answer. (2 marks)"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "The learner is asked to identify the cell type and give a reason. The diagnostic step is to check whether they notice the external power source in the diagram. I will ask one short question about the electrode connections without revealing the answer.",
      "content": "Look at the diagram connections: are the carbon electrodes attached to a battery or DC power supply, or are they joined directly to each other by a wire? Tell me what you see, and I will help you name the cell."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The electrodes are connected to a battery/DC power supply."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "The learner correctly identified the battery/DC power supply, which is the key feature for an electrolytic cell. I can now give the consolidated final answer matching the memo, break down the two-mark allocation, and add an exam tip.",
      "content": "Electrolytic, because it uses a power source/battery to convert electrical energy to chemical energy.\n\n### 📖 Formula Breakdown (How It Works):\n* **The Rule:** A cell with an external power source/battery is **electrolytic**; a cell without one (spontaneous reaction) is **galvanic**.\n* **What the parts mean:**\n  * **External power source:** a battery or DC supply that forces electrons through the circuit.\n  * **Electrical energy → chemical energy:** electricity drives a reaction that would not happen on its own.\n* **Why we use it:** The mark scheme awards one mark for the cell name and one mark for the reason. Spotting the battery gives you both marks.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Always scan the diagram for a battery symbol first. If one is present, the cell is electrolytic. Do not switch to galvanic just because the chemicals look familiar."
    }
  ],
  "meta": {
    "strategy_used": "exam_technique",
    "final_answer": "Electrolytic, because it uses a power source/battery to convert electrical energy to chemical energy.",
    "verify_code": "print(\"Electrolytic, because it uses a power source/battery to convert electrical energy to chemical energy.\")",
